// Day 26 — p50/p95/p99 by endpoint.
//
// THREE THINGS IN HERE ARE NOT DECORATION, and a query without them reads
// convincingly while being wrong.
//
// 1. HEALTH PROBES ARE EXCLUDED. Container Apps calls /health/live and
//    /health/ready every 10 seconds per replica, forever. They are the
//    fastest endpoints in the app and, on anything but heavy traffic, the
//    most numerous by an order of magnitude — so leaving them in drags every
//    aggregate toward "everything is fast" and buries the endpoints a user
//    actually waits on. They are excluded here rather than filtered by the
//    reader afterwards, because a number that is quietly wrong is worse than
//    one that is missing.
//
// 2. THE REQUEST COUNT IS SHOWN NEXT TO THE PERCENTILE. A p99 over four
//    requests is the slowest of four requests. It is not a tail latency and
//    treating it as one produces confident nonsense. The `requests >= 5`
//    floor removes the worst of it; the column is there so the reader can
//    judge the rest.
//
// 3. sum(ItemCount), NOT count(). Application Insights sampling drops
//    events and records the multiplier in ItemCount — one stored row can
//    represent ten real requests. count() counts rows and silently
//    under-reports as soon as sampling turns on. Sampling is off in this
//    deployment today, which is exactly why it is easy to write count() and
//    not notice for months.
//
// Name is the ROUTE TEMPLATE ("GET /api/quotes/{id}"), not the raw URL, so
// /api/quotes/1 and /api/quotes/2 aggregate. Grouping by URL instead is the
// classic cardinality explosion: thousands of one-request groups, no signal.
AppRequests
| where TimeGenerated > ago(24h)
| where Name !startswith "GET /health"
| summarize
    requests = sum(ItemCount),
    p50      = round(percentile(DurationMs, 50), 1),
    p95      = round(percentile(DurationMs, 95), 1),
    p99      = round(percentile(DurationMs, 99), 1),
    failures = sumif(ItemCount, Success == false)
    by Endpoint = Name
| extend failureRatePct = round(100.0 * failures / requests, 2)
| where requests >= 5
| project Endpoint, requests, p50, p95, p99, failures, failureRatePct
| order by p99 desc
